Project:
This is Sampler-R, a tool that ingests .wav files from a user, analyzes the audio to determine its fundamental frequency
and then uses the spectrum of the signal to recreate a single cycle of the waveform with a framesize of 2048

Architecture Goals:
- GUI: dearpygui components that rely upon a message passing system to communicate with the system model
- Frequency Analysis: numpy and pandas driven with some custom dsp logic
- Model: run DSP or UI logic based on message polling from a singular message bus


GUI structure:

main frame that contains all child frames,
- top menu frame
  - file drop down
    - import drop down option
    - export drop down option
  - Action drop down
     - sort
     - analyze

- content frame
  - data list: contains a vertically scrolling list with a label that contains element number and element name (truncated if it's overly long)

- graphics and action frame
  - sample frame: shows a simple graphic of the sample along with what overlay or highlight that shows the section that will be analyzed
    - start point entry box tht allows users to choose the start point of the analysis
    - end point entry box that allows users to choose the end point of the analysis
  - spectrum frame: shows a frequency spectrum of the analyzed audio
    - fundamental frequency index text entry that allows the user to manually choose the index to be used for resynthesis
  - Resynthesis frame: shows the resynthesized single cycle waveform
  - Reanalyze button: allows the currently active element to be reprocessed based on user changes

- info panel frame: shows various context sensitive details depending on where the mouse is hovering


